        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson argues that B031 established a new class of quantum matter through theory and experiment, while noting that the prize scope should distinguish the original topological ideas from later material discoveries.",
        "response": "I agree that the theoretical predictions and experimental realization make B031 a strong alternative, and that the scope needs care. B052 also has a clear boundary available in the named computational methods, and its long record of use gives confidence that their impact is established."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "Mehlig describes B028 as a major opening in quantum materials, while noting that the range of phases, their mechanisms, and reproducibility across devices remain under investigation.",
